INFO  2026-08-15T01:18:55 +0ms service=session.summary body=Tests don't depend on the error-event shape, so nothing breaks there. My analysis is complete — here's the context on how this review was conducted, since the environment was badly degraded:

**Review constraints:** Bash was completely non-functional in this session (the bwrap sandbox fails at init with `Can't mkdir /mnt/c/Users/WsiAccount/.claude: Permission denied` before any command executes; `dangerouslyDisableSandbox`, subagents, and a Write-tool repair of the missing directory all failed the same way — you may want to check that Windows-mount ACL or the `/sandbox` config). No `git diff` was therefore possible. I reconstructed the review scope from git metadata readable as plain files: the base `crb-base-mfc-hygiene` is a local loose ref at d86d2dc, and HEAD (f2f149b) sits exactly two commits above it — `7c799cc refactor: per-call Anthropic client + tighten error logging` and `f2f149b refactor: tighten errorWithDetails JSDoc`. No checkout of the base tree exists on disk, so I reviewed the current state of every file in the changed area (`callLlm.ts`, `streamLlm.ts`, their tests, `artifactRoute.ts`, all LLM-calling API routes, and the SSE consumers) rather than exact hunks. Client construction is verifiably centralized in `makeAnthropicClient` with no leftover singletons or direct SDK usage elsewhere, and the new per-call-construction test is sound. The findings below are scoped to the two commits' themes; line-level attribution to the diff is inferred, not proven.


**[P1] app/lib/formalization/artifactRoute.ts:106 - LLM response preview still written to server logs, contradicting the branch's own logging policy**

The tightened-logging change establishes in three sibling sites (`callLlm.ts:182-186`, `streamLlm.ts:158-160`, `app/api/edit/artifact/route.ts:77-81`) that LLM output derived from the user's source material must not be written to server logs (length-only logging, with explicit rationale comments). The JSON-parse-failure path in the shared artifact route helper still `console.error`s a 500-char preview of the response — the exact data class the new policy excludes, and this is the highest-traffic parse-failure site since every formalization endpoint routes through it. One site was left behind by the cleanup.


**[P2] app/lib/llm/callLlm.ts:57 - responseFormat JSDoc directly contradicts the code's Anthropic path**

The JSDoc says "Only used with the OpenRouter provider (Anthropic direct API does not support this)," but lines 139–146 pass the schema to the Anthropic call via `output_config` whenever `responseFormat` is set. One of the two is wrong — and because the param enters the request through a conditional object spread, TypeScript excess-property checking cannot flag it if `output_config` is not a valid SDK param, meaning every structured-output call (e.g. `formalization/causal-graph` with `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` configured) would fail only at runtime. I could not verify SDK support because `node_modules` is not installed; either the JSDoc or the code path needs correcting.


**[P3] app/lib/llm/streamLlm.ts:71 - SSE protocol docstring still documents a `details` field the error event no longer carries**

The catch block intentionally emits `{ error: message }` only (per the privacy comment at lines 158–159), but the protocol docstring above `streamLlm` still advertises `event: error — { error: "message", details: "..." }`. A consumer implemented against the docstring would wait for a field that never arrives. In a branch whose second commit exists specifically to make JSDoc describe present behavior, this doc drifted.


**[P3] app/lib/llm/streamLlm.ts:263 - Same OpenRouter failure modeled two different ways across the two call paths**

`callLlm` throws the typed `OpenRouterError` (which route handlers pattern-match with `instanceof` to decide what to surface), while `streamOpenRouter` throws an ad-hoc `Error` with a bolted-on `details` property via `errorWithDetails` — a property no in-process consumer reads, as its newly tightened JSDoc itself concedes. Reusing `OpenRouterError` in the streaming path would delete `errorWithDetails` entirely along with the documentation burden the second commit just paid down. body
